# Git LFS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE REPOSITORY IS IN A DELIBERATE MIXED STATE. READ THIS BEFORE DEBUGGING IT.
#
# LFS was enabled at v0.3-cleanup WITHOUT migrating existing history. Every
# binary committed before that point is still a normal git blob, and stays that
# way until the file is next modified. So at any moment some PNGs are LFS
# pointers and some are ordinary blobs, and that is correct, not a mistake.
#
# Why not migrate: rewriting history would change every commit SHA, break the
# v0.3-cleanup tag and every existing clone, to reclaim ~3.3 MB. The reason LFS
# is here at all is what comes NEXT - a per-theme, per-tile golden matrix
# (13 tile types x states x themes) that will add far more binary weight than
# the current baseline.
#
# To check what a given file actually is:
#     git lfs ls-files                 # everything currently in LFS
#     git cat-file -p HEAD:<path> | head -1
#         "version https://git-lfs.github.com/spec/v1"  -> LFS pointer
#         PNG header bytes                              -> ordinary blob
#
# NEW CLONES MUST RUN `git lfs install` ONCE. Without it the working tree gets
# pointer text files instead of images, and the golden comparison would be
# reading 130-byte text files as PNGs. PixelUtil.Load rejects pointer files
# explicitly with a loud error rather than failing obscurely - see its guard.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Images
*.png  filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.PNG  filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.jpg  filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
